1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,620
We have time for dinner at the neighborhood
restaurant.

2
00:00:04,870 --> 00:00:07,700
Everyone can choose something they enjoy.

3
00:00:07,950 --> 00:00:11,210
I will be our extremely prepared diner.

4
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:18,330
Can we look at a menu?

5
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:21,410
Will there be room for six?

6
00:00:21,660 --> 00:00:24,920
We will ask for a table together.

7
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:33,760
Esteemed keeper of dinner, we humbly request—

8
00:00:34,010 --> 00:00:36,410
A simple question will work.

9
00:00:36,660 --> 00:00:39,490
I may have overdressed the sentence.

10
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:47,900
Will everything be too hot?

11
00:00:48,150 --> 00:00:53,130
We can ask, and let food cool when it needs
to.

12
00:00:53,380 --> 00:00:55,780
Clear questions. I am ready.

13
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:04,190
Eighty dollars for the meal, tax, and tip.

14
00:01:04,440 --> 00:01:07,700
We will check the prices before ordering.

15
00:01:07,950 --> 00:01:10,780
A budget that includes the ending.

16
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:18,760
Perhaps a dessert taller than this kitchen—

17
00:01:19,010 --> 00:01:22,270
We have not seen the menu yet.

18
00:01:22,520 --> 00:01:24,920
Let us start with dinner.

19
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:32,470
I can check prices.

20
00:01:32,720 --> 00:01:35,980
I want to choose my own dinner.

21
00:01:36,230 --> 00:01:39,920
Of course. Max can ask for water too.

22
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:47,900
I have shortened my speech.

23
00:01:48,150 --> 00:01:49,950
How short?

24
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:54,320
Good evening. That should get us through the
door.

25
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:02,300
Good evening.

26
00:02:02,550 --> 00:02:04,950
That was an excellent length.

27
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:08,460
We all fit through the door too.

28
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:19,190
Could we have a table for six, please?

29
00:02:19,440 --> 00:02:23,130
Certainly. The table by the window is ready.

30
00:02:23,380 --> 00:02:25,180
Thank you.

31
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:34,190
Stay beside me. This aisle is for everyone.

32
00:02:34,440 --> 00:02:37,270
I will wait for Leo's chair.

33
00:02:37,520 --> 00:02:39,490
No chair traffic jam.

34
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:47,470
Three on this side.

35
00:02:47,720 --> 00:02:50,120
Three on the window side.

36
00:02:50,370 --> 00:02:54,490
A table with exactly the right audience for
dinner.

37
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:03,760
Here are your menus. Take your time.

38
00:03:04,010 --> 00:03:05,810
Thank you.

39
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:08,030
We will choose together.

40
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:19,190
Do I have to read the whole book?

41
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:22,700
Only the parts that help you choose.

42
00:03:22,950 --> 00:03:25,780
The dinner section is right here.

43
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:32,900
Could we have water, please?

44
00:03:33,150 --> 00:03:35,980
Of course. Six glasses of water.

45
00:03:36,230 --> 00:03:39,920
My speech has been defeated by six words.

46
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:48,330
Your water. There is no charge.

47
00:03:48,580 --> 00:03:50,380
Thank you.

48
00:03:50,630 --> 00:03:53,890
Mine has its own safe parking place.

49
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:02,470
Appetizers, main courses, desserts.

50
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:05,980
I am ready for a main course.

51
00:04:06,230 --> 00:04:10,350
Then our dinner can begin in the middle
section.

52
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:18,760
The vegetable pasta sounds good. Twelve
dollars.

53
00:04:19,010 --> 00:04:21,410
With the vegetables listed here?

54
00:04:21,660 --> 00:04:24,920
Yes. That is the one I want.

55
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:33,330
Grilled chicken with rice for me.

56
00:04:33,580 --> 00:04:36,840
One main course, with the rice included?

57
00:04:37,090 --> 00:04:39,060
Exactly. Fourteen dollars together.

58
00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:48,330
I would like the cheese sandwich.

59
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:51,410
You can tell the server yourself.

60
00:04:51,660 --> 00:04:55,780
Eight dollars. I have its place in our plan.

61
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:03,760
Does the baked potato include the vegetables?

62
00:05:04,010 --> 00:05:06,410
Yes. The filling is included.

63
00:05:06,660 --> 00:05:09,490
Then I would like that, please.

64
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:18,760
There is a smaller chicken and rice.

65
00:05:19,010 --> 00:05:21,410
That can be your dinner.

66
00:05:21,660 --> 00:05:26,210
That one, please. I like a plate made for me.

67
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:33,760
The tomato soup looks right for me.

68
00:05:34,010 --> 00:05:37,270
What kind of flavor would you enjoy?

69
00:05:37,520 --> 00:05:39,490
Something comforting. And hot.

70
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:48,760
I would like the soup hot, please.

71
00:05:49,010 --> 00:05:53,130
Do you mean its temperature, or a spicy
flavor?

72
00:05:53,380 --> 00:05:56,210
Those are different kinds of hot?

73
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:02,470
This pepper means spicy.

74
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:05,550
I was thinking of warm soup.

75
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:09,060
Then we should say both things clearly.

76
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:18,330
Should I rescue Dad with water?

77
00:06:18,580 --> 00:06:20,550
Nothing spicy has arrived.

78
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:24,920
I need a better sentence, not a rescue team.

79
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:33,760
Mild tomato soup, please. Warm, not extra-hot.

80
00:06:34,010 --> 00:06:35,980
Certainly. No chili added.

81
00:06:36,230 --> 00:06:39,490
That tells us exactly what you want.

82
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:49,620
Could we change the note before you send it?

83
00:06:49,870 --> 00:06:53,560
Of course. It now says mild and warm.

84
00:06:53,810 --> 00:06:56,210
No guessing reaches the kitchen.

85
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:03,330
One meal for each of us.

86
00:07:03,580 --> 00:07:07,700
My chicken plate and Max's smaller plate are
separate.

87
00:07:07,950 --> 00:07:11,640
And my soup is dinner, not an appetizer.

88
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:18,330
Fifty-eight dollars for the six meals.

89
00:07:18,580 --> 00:07:20,550
Before tax and tip.

90
00:07:20,800 --> 00:07:25,350
Then the calculator has one more part of the
story.

91
00:07:30,500 --> 00:07:33,760
This menu lists ten percent sales tax.

92
00:07:34,010 --> 00:07:36,410
That adds five dollars eighty.

93
00:07:36,660 --> 00:07:40,780
Sixty-three eighty before our tip. Still room
to plan.

94
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:48,330
Let us plan a ten-dollar tip.

95
00:07:48,580 --> 00:07:50,550
That fits our budget.

96
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:54,490
Seventy-three eighty altogether. Six twenty
stays with us.

97
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:02,300
Cheese sandwich, please.

98
00:08:02,550 --> 00:08:05,380
The baked potato with its vegetables.

99
00:08:05,630 --> 00:08:08,460
The children's chicken and rice, please.

100
00:08:15,500 --> 00:08:17,900
Vegetable pasta for me, please.

101
00:08:18,150 --> 00:08:20,550
The adult chicken and rice.

102
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:24,920
Mild tomato soup, warm rather than extra-hot.
Thank you.

103
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:33,330
Any ingredient restrictions I should flag?

104
00:08:33,580 --> 00:08:37,270
We checked the listed ingredients for our
family.

105
00:08:37,520 --> 00:08:40,780
No changes to this order, thank you.

106
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:51,340
Six mains, with the soup mild and warm. I will
send this now.

107
00:08:51,590 --> 00:08:55,280
Thank you. That was easier than my speech.

108
00:09:00,500 --> 00:09:04,620
Does dinner need a quiet minute like pancake
batter?

109
00:09:04,870 --> 00:09:07,270
It needs time to cook.

110
00:09:07,520 --> 00:09:10,780
We are getting good at that part.

111
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:18,330
And now, the very patient fork.

112
00:09:18,580 --> 00:09:22,270
It has nothing to say until dinner arrives.

113
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:24,490
A beautifully quiet introduction.

114
00:09:30,500 --> 00:09:33,760
Can mild food still be too hot?

115
00:09:34,010 --> 00:09:37,270
Yes. Mild describes flavor. Temperature is
different.

116
00:09:37,520 --> 00:09:41,210
That was the missing half of my sentence.

117
00:09:45,500 --> 00:09:49,620
I guessed a whole breakfast from one word
once.

118
00:09:49,870 --> 00:09:51,840
Context helped then too.

119
00:09:52,090 --> 00:09:55,780
This time you asked before anything went
wrong.

120
00:10:00,500 --> 00:10:03,330
Are we missing the appetizer part?

121
00:10:03,580 --> 00:10:05,980
We chose dinner without one.

122
00:10:06,230 --> 00:10:10,780
The menu is a choice, not a list to finish.

123
00:10:15,500 --> 00:10:18,760
I prepared a request for more water.

124
00:10:19,010 --> 00:10:21,410
Your glass still has plenty.

125
00:10:21,660 --> 00:10:25,350
Then my request can wait beside my speech.

126
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:33,760
Let us leave room for the server.

127
00:10:34,010 --> 00:10:36,410
My hands can wait here.

128
00:10:36,660 --> 00:10:39,920
Mine too. Dinner gets a clear landing.

129
00:10:45,500 --> 00:10:49,190
Vegetable pasta, and the adult chicken and
rice.

130
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:51,840
That is mine, thank you.

131
00:10:52,090 --> 00:10:54,490
And this one is mine.

132
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:02,300
My cheese sandwich.

133
00:11:02,550 --> 00:11:05,810
And the baked potato I asked about.

134
00:11:06,060 --> 00:11:10,610
Keep the hot plate on the table while it
cools.

135
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:19,620
Mild tomato soup, and the children's chicken
and rice.

136
00:11:19,870 --> 00:11:21,670
Thank you.

137
00:11:21,920 --> 00:11:25,610
We will check the temperature before we begin.

138
00:11:30,500 --> 00:11:32,900
Six orders, six correct dinners.

139
00:11:33,150 --> 00:11:35,550
Mine has the vegetables included.

140
00:11:35,800 --> 00:11:39,920
And mine has a smaller plate, just as
promised.

141
00:11:45,500 --> 00:11:48,330
I will check a little first.

142
00:11:48,580 --> 00:11:52,700
And we let it cool if it needs to.

143
00:11:52,950 --> 00:11:55,780
Even when the flavor is mild.

144
00:12:00,500 --> 00:12:02,900
Is that what you wanted?

145
00:12:03,150 --> 00:12:05,550
Yes. Mild flavor, comfortably warm.

146
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:09,920
A much better description than one very busy
word.

147
00:12:15,500 --> 00:12:17,900
The middle needs another moment.

148
00:12:18,150 --> 00:12:19,950
You can wait.

149
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:24,320
Dinner is not a race to the hottest bite.

150
00:12:30,500 --> 00:12:32,470
How is your dinner?

151
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:36,840
Good. My napkin has more work than your
speech.

152
00:12:37,090 --> 00:12:40,350
It came prepared for the right job.

153
00:12:45,500 --> 00:12:48,330
I liked saying my own order.

154
00:12:48,580 --> 00:12:50,980
You knew what you wanted.

155
00:12:51,230 --> 00:12:54,920
And I liked asking what came with mine.

156
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:04,190
The server saved my dinner with one question.

157
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:07,270
They gave you room to explain.

158
00:13:07,520 --> 00:13:10,780
And you used it. That worked well.

159
00:13:15,500 --> 00:13:18,760
Will we ever hear your big speech?

160
00:13:19,010 --> 00:13:23,130
It is enjoying a quiet dinner in my pocket.

161
00:13:23,380 --> 00:13:25,350
A very well-behaved speech.

162
00:13:30,500 --> 00:13:33,760
The library is open tomorrow, isn't it?

163
00:13:34,010 --> 00:13:36,840
We can check the hours later.

164
00:13:37,090 --> 00:13:39,920
Tonight we can finish dinner together.

165
00:13:45,500 --> 00:13:47,900
No rescue needed after all.

166
00:13:48,150 --> 00:13:50,550
Just a drink with dinner.

167
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:54,490
And a safe place to put it back.

168
00:14:00,500 --> 00:14:03,330
We can take a comfortable pause.

169
00:14:03,580 --> 00:14:07,700
I would like to save the rest of mine.

170
00:14:07,950 --> 00:14:11,640
Then we can ask for a takeout box.

171
00:14:15,500 --> 00:14:18,760
Could we have one takeout box, please?

172
00:14:19,010 --> 00:14:20,810
Certainly.

173
00:14:21,060 --> 00:14:25,610
For the rest of Max's dinner, not a second
dinner.

174
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:32,300
Here you are.

175
00:14:32,550 --> 00:14:34,350
Thank you.

176
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:38,720
An empty box waiting for food we already have.

177
00:14:45,500 --> 00:14:48,330
Your remaining dinner goes in once.

178
00:14:48,580 --> 00:14:51,410
So my plate is empty now.

179
00:14:51,660 --> 00:14:55,350
And the box has the part you saved.

180
00:15:00,500 --> 00:15:04,620
We will go straight home and refrigerate this
promptly.

181
00:15:04,870 --> 00:15:06,670
No extra stops.

182
00:15:06,920 --> 00:15:10,180
My dinner has a sensible travel plan.

183
00:15:15,500 --> 00:15:17,300
I am finished.

184
00:15:17,550 --> 00:15:19,350
Me too.

185
00:15:19,600 --> 00:15:24,580
Then we can ask for the check when everyone is
ready.

186
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:34,190
My imaginary tall dessert can stay imaginary
tonight.

187
00:15:34,440 --> 00:15:36,410
I am satisfied too.

188
00:15:36,660 --> 00:15:40,350
Then our order is complete as it is.

189
00:15:45,500 --> 00:15:48,330
Could we have the check, please?

190
00:15:48,580 --> 00:15:51,840
Of course. I will bring it over.

191
00:15:52,090 --> 00:15:53,890
Thank you.

192
00:16:00,500 --> 00:16:03,330
This box is coming with us.

193
00:16:03,580 --> 00:16:06,840
Of course. I will leave it here.

194
00:16:07,090 --> 00:16:09,490
It has its own traveler.

195
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:17,470
Here is your check.

196
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:19,520
Thank you.

197
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:22,600
May I help check the numbers?

198
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:34,190
Six meals. No extra soup, starter, or dessert.

199
00:16:34,440 --> 00:16:36,410
And water is free.

200
00:16:36,660 --> 00:16:40,780
The order on paper matches the dinner we had.

201
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:47,470
Fifty-eight plus five eighty.

202
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:49,520
Sixty-three eighty.

203
00:16:49,770 --> 00:16:54,320
Our planned tip is separate. Good to check
before paying.

204
00:17:00,500 --> 00:17:04,190
Shall we keep the ten-dollar tip we planned?

205
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:06,240
Yes.

206
00:17:06,490 --> 00:17:10,180
Seventy-three eighty altogether. Still inside
our eighty-dollar plan.

207
00:17:15,500 --> 00:17:17,900
Does your speech pay too?

208
00:17:18,150 --> 00:17:21,410
No. Just the money in this wallet.

209
00:17:21,660 --> 00:17:24,490
Then the speech can keep resting.

210
00:17:30,500 --> 00:17:34,190
Do I pay here or at the counter?

211
00:17:34,440 --> 00:17:36,840
At the service counter, please.

212
00:17:37,090 --> 00:17:40,350
We will wait here with the children.

213
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:47,900
I will be right back.

214
00:17:48,150 --> 00:17:50,120
We will be here.

215
00:17:50,370 --> 00:17:54,060
And our takeout traveler is staying with me.

216
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:02,300
Eighty dollars, please.

217
00:18:02,550 --> 00:18:07,100
Thank you. Your change is sixteen dollars and
twenty cents.

218
00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:18,760
Sixteen twenty in change, before the tip.

219
00:18:19,010 --> 00:18:20,810
That's right.

220
00:18:21,060 --> 00:18:22,860
Thank you.

221
00:18:30,500 --> 00:18:35,910
This ten dollars is a tip. Thank you for
checking my order.

222
00:18:36,160 --> 00:18:38,990
Thank you. Have a lovely evening.

223
00:18:45,500 --> 00:18:49,190
Receipt, remaining change, and a much smaller
speech.

224
00:18:49,440 --> 00:18:52,270
All set. Thank you for coming.

225
00:19:00,500 --> 00:19:02,300
Everyone ready?

226
00:19:02,550 --> 00:19:04,950
One box, all our people.

227
00:19:05,200 --> 00:19:08,460
And no speech left on the table.

228
00:19:15,500 --> 00:19:17,900
What stayed in the budget?

229
00:19:18,150 --> 00:19:20,980
Six twenty after the ten-dollar tip.

230
00:19:21,230 --> 00:19:25,350
Seventy-three eighty spent. The numbers reach
the same ending.

231
00:19:30,500 --> 00:19:33,760
What will your next big speech be?

232
00:19:34,010 --> 00:19:36,840
Could I have some water, please?

233
00:19:37,090 --> 00:19:40,350
Perfect. Now straight home with our box.

234
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:49,190
A warm dinner and a very clear evening.

235
00:19:49,440 --> 00:19:51,240
Good questions helped.

236
00:19:51,490 --> 00:19:54,750
And nobody had to eat a speech.
